You don't think that's
too stagey?


00:20:27.689 --> 00:20:29.477
Well, the catholic church
has never shied away


00:20:29.557 --> 00:20:30.645
from a little pageantry.


00:20:30.725 --> 00:20:31.713
Yeah...


00:20:31.793 --> 00:20:33.715
I've seen the crucifix.


00:20:33.795 --> 00:20:35.795
That's not really what I
was referring... too soon?


00:20:36.965 --> 00:20:38.525
That was kind of too soon.


00:20:40.367 --> 00:20:43.224
You gotta wait till
at least 3,000 years.


00:20:43.304 --> 00:20:46.227
But, I mean, come on.
They put makeup on Jesus.


00:20:46.307 --> 00:20:47.595
No, they don't.
Yeah, they do.


00:20:47.675 --> 00:20:49.164
When do they put makeup on
Jesus?


00:20:49.244 --> 00:20:50.431
Have you looked at any of
the crucifixes


00:20:50.511 --> 00:20:51.766
where he's got kind,
like, blush on


00:20:51.846 --> 00:20:53.234
and some eyeliner?


00:20:53.314 --> 00:20:55.470
- It's hot in the sun.
- Um, no.


00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:57.438
They're making him look pretty.


00:20:57.518 --> 00:21:00.175
He looks like a woman
in some of those.


00:21:00.255 --> 00:21:01.776
Which is not all that weird


00:21:01.856 --> 00:21:03.945
because, you know,
maybe... who knows?


00:21:04.025 --> 00:21:06.247
"Hey-Soos" would be glad
that you figured it out.


00:21:06.327 --> 00:21:07.927
That's how you say
his name in Spanish...


00:21:17.604 --> 00:21:19.928
"He... he answereth and saith
unto them,


00:21:20.008 --> 00:21:24.332
"'let him that hath two coats
impart to him that hath none.


00:21:24.412 --> 00:21:26.812
And let him
that hath meat...'"


00:21:27.514 --> 00:21:28.970
baby, do the same.


00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.483
Luke 3:11.


00:21:31.285 --> 00:21:32.485
How do you like me now?


00:21:33.787 --> 00:21:35.788
Father. Father.


00:21:40.594 --> 00:21:42.217
No run today?


00:21:42.297 --> 00:21:43.651
I guess I slept in.


00:21:43.731 --> 00:21:45.553
- Is everything okay?
- Y-yeah, yeah.


00:21:45.633 --> 00:21:47.566
No, yeah. Just tired.


00:21:48.835 --> 00:21:49.757
Victor...


00:21:49.837 --> 00:21:52.527
Surely you have a verse in there


00:21:52.607 --> 00:21:54.362
about the evils of hitting
the snooze button.


00:21:54.442 --> 00:21:57.432
Mm-hm. Are the late Fridays
a bit too much?


00:21:57.512 --> 00:21:59.834
No, not at all.
I'll talk to the bishop.


00:21:59.914 --> 00:22:01.836
No, I-i... you were right.


00:22:01.916 --> 00:22:03.671
It's been... it's been really...


00:22:03.751 --> 00:22:06.519
It's good. It's very good.
For me.


00:22:07.621 --> 00:22:08.810
Daniel...
You know, we get to reach out


00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.356
to different, uh...


00:22:11.591 --> 00:22:12.725
So yeah.


00:22:14.328 --> 00:22:15.361
Yeah.


00:22:19.833 --> 00:22:22.368
Okay.


00:22:25.972 --> 00:22:28.329
My problem is that he'll tell
his mother


00:22:28.409 --> 00:22:30.331
every little detail about
our life


00:22:30.411 --> 00:22:34.035
but with me, it's just
I think that he has a problem


00:22:34.115 --> 00:22:35.670
with communication.


00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:37.605
And that is what he really needs
to work on.


00:22:37.685 --> 00:22:40.408
And he knows that already
because I tell him all the time,


00:22:40.488 --> 00:22:43.011
but he just goes about his day
like he doesn't even hear me,


00:22:43.091 --> 00:22:45.647
which, you can imagine,
doesn't feel good


00:22:45.727 --> 00:22:48.049
when I'm trying to express
my feelings,


00:22:48.129 --> 00:22:52.320
which I believe is at the core of
the problem with the marriage,


00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.790
not to say that we don't have
a good marriage, because we do.


00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:59.827
It's just I thought that if we
talked to someone within the church,


00:22:59.907 --> 00:23:03.509
it might better open up the lines
of communication between...


00:23:04.044 --> 00:23:05.478
Father!
Yes.


00:23:06.380 --> 00:23:07.680
Yes what?


00:23:12.119 --> 00:23:14.520
Yes, what he said. Yes.


00:23:19.693 --> 00:23:20.915
Yes, I apologized.


00:23:20.995 --> 00:23:23.751
I listened to her
for another hour...


00:23:23.831 --> 00:23:24.997
Without interruption...


00:23:25.866 --> 00:23:27.388
And of course I assured her


00:23:27.468 --> 00:23:28.756
that it would
never happen again.


00:23:28.836 --> 00:23:30.503
This is not like you.


00:23:31.071 --> 00:23:32.171
I know.


00:23:33.073 --> 00:23:35.074
We've discussed the


00:23:36.009 --> 00:23:38.010
importance of detail.


00:23:39.946 --> 00:23:42.770
It's the reason why
I do even this,


00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:46.786
instead of letting
some sacristan housewife...


00:23:47.554 --> 00:23:48.843
God bless them...


00:23:48.923 --> 00:23:52.347
Improperly dress my alter.


00:23:52.427 --> 00:23:53.881
I'm sorry, father.


00:23:53.961 --> 00:23:56.028
Do you feel his presence,
Daniel?


00:23:56.763 --> 00:23:58.798
Yes, of course. Always.


00:24:01.568 --> 00:24:02.868
It's okay to say no.


00:24:03.637 --> 00:24:04.637
Yeah, I know.


00:24:08.074 --> 00:24:09.697
Wait a minute.
How is it okay?


00:24:09.777 --> 00:24:12.367
This isn't magic.
We are not special.


00:24:12.447 --> 00:24:16.916
Nor do we have
some privileged access to god.


00:24:18.051 --> 00:24:21.520
We are men who chose to serve.


00:24:22.456 --> 00:24:25.046
Whether or not we see


00:24:25.126 --> 00:24:28.449
or hear or feel him


00:24:28.529 --> 00:24:30.796
at any given time
is not the point.


00:24:31.965 --> 00:24:34.700
Our job is
to be ever present for him.


00:24:35.869 --> 00:24:38.971
The day to day,
the minute to minute.


00:24:39.873 --> 00:24:41.140
This moment.


00:24:41.942 --> 00:24:42.942
Now.


00:24:43.543 --> 00:24:44.643
The details?


00:24:45.078 --> 00:24:46.245
Exactly.


00:24:49.716 --> 00:24:50.749
Do you?


00:24:51.651 --> 00:24:52.718
Do I what?


00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:55.020
See god?


00:24:56.623 --> 00:24:57.790
Yes.


00:24:59.793 --> 00:25:00.960
Sometimes.


00:25:43.837 --> 00:25:45.092
- A-2.
- Miss.


00:25:45.172 --> 00:25:46.894
Really?


00:25:46.974 --> 00:25:48.496
I don't cheat at battleship,


00:25:48.576 --> 00:25:49.764
and if I was going to start,


00:25:49.844 --> 00:25:51.644
it wouldn't be in this building.


00:25:52.078 --> 00:25:53.812
Oh, and, um...


00:25:54.881 --> 00:25:57.883
C-6, by the way.


00:25:59.986 --> 00:26:01.809
You sunk my battleship.


00:26:01.889 --> 00:26:05.024
Oh, three losses in a row.


00:26:05.325 --> 00:26:06.781
Ouch.


00:26:06.861 --> 00:26:08.616
I wasn't really counting.


00:26:08.696 --> 00:26:11.564
Not to be, you know, but I'm...


00:26:12.599 --> 00:26:14.767
I'm totally dominating
this confession.


00:26:19.039 --> 00:26:20.072
What?


00:26:21.074 --> 00:26:22.308
You haven't really...


00:26:23.310 --> 00:26:25.066
I mean,


00:26:25.146 --> 00:26:26.968
I don't feel like
I'm really doing my job here.


00:26:27.048 --> 00:26:28.603
I know I'm not, actually.


00:26:28.683 --> 00:26:29.971
Do you want me
to confess something?


00:26:30.051 --> 00:26:31.083
No.


00:26:32.052 --> 00:26:33.808
I mean, not unless you want to.


00:26:33.888 --> 00:26:35.810
I don't want you to feel
like it's required.


00:26:35.890 --> 00:26:38.012
There is something.


00:26:38.092 --> 00:26:39.224
What?


00:26:43.363 --> 00:26:44.619
You can say anything.


00:26:44.699 --> 00:26:45.699
I know, but...


00:26:46.933 --> 00:26:48.689
I'm just afraid that
if I tell you,


00:26:48.769 --> 00:26:51.092
I don't know,
things might change.


00:26:51.172 --> 00:26:53.261
What things?
Just... things...


00:26:53.341 --> 00:26:54.640
Between us.


00:26:57.844 --> 00:26:58.944
Jane...


00:26:59.980 --> 00:27:01.981
Promise you won't hate me?


00:27:03.984 --> 00:27:05.017
I promise.


00:27:06.019 --> 00:27:06.974
Thing is...


00:27:07.054 --> 00:27:10.177
I've been trying to find a way
to say this all night.


00:27:10.257 --> 00:27:11.957
I just... oh, I don't know.


00:27:12.892 --> 00:27:13.926
I...


00:27:15.195 --> 00:27:16.228
I...


00:27:18.098 --> 00:27:20.199
I totally cheated.


00:27:22.268 --> 00:27:23.658
What?


00:27:23.738 --> 00:27:25.226
The first game
was actually close,


00:27:25.306 --> 00:27:27.640
and I just... I lied a bit.


00:27:28.875 --> 00:27:31.143
Didn't even place my ships
in the next two.


00:27:33.313 --> 00:27:34.647
You hate me?


00:27:35.215 --> 00:27:36.270
Why would I hate you?


00:27:36.350 --> 00:27:37.805
Just seems like


00:27:37.885 --> 00:27:39.818
I'm always
sitting on my... you know...


00:27:40.353 --> 00:27:42.921
Sinner half and...


00:27:43.890 --> 00:27:45.257
You have to listen to all
of my...


00:27:46.893 --> 00:27:47.882
What about you?


00:27:47.962 --> 00:27:48.916
Me?


00:27:48.996 --> 00:27:51.352
You ever get a chance to sit on
this side?


00:27:51.432 --> 00:27:53.287
You know, get stuff off
your chest?


00:27:53.367 --> 00:27:55.656
Priests go to confession, too.


00:27:55.736 --> 00:27:59.193
But you only confess
to other priests, right?


00:27:59.273 --> 00:28:00.962
That's sort of how it works.


00:28:01.042 --> 00:28:03.809
Well, what if you wanted
to confess to someone else?


00:28:04.678 --> 00:28:05.833
I don't know what you mean.


00:28:05.913 --> 00:28:08.202
To me, for example.


00:28:08.282 --> 00:28:11.238
I... don't think that's
a very good idea.


00:28:11.318 --> 00:28:13.908
It doesn't have to be juicy
or anything.


00:28:13.988 --> 00:28:15.821
Just something real.


00:28:17.190 --> 00:28:20.392
To a normal, non-priesty person.


00:28:23.997 --> 00:28:25.820
Might be good for you.
I don't think that...


00:28:25.900 --> 00:28:28.055
Awesome. Switch me.


00:28:28.135 --> 00:28:30.169
Jane? Jane? Jane.


00:28:35.008 --> 00:28:37.976
What is this? It's a gift.
Me to you.


00:28:38.712 --> 00:28:39.867
I don't understand.


00:28:39.947 --> 00:28:41.002
You go in there, you know,


00:28:41.082 --> 00:28:42.837
on the sinner side,


00:28:42.917 --> 00:28:44.972
and just for a few minutes
you get to be a normal person,


00:28:45.052 --> 00:28:47.274
not somebody
who's gotta do everything right.


00:28:47.354 --> 00:28:50.978
Not somebody who's supposed to have any
sort of profound existential insights,


00:28:51.058 --> 00:28:54.827
and certainly not someone who's gotta
listen to me ramble on about my...


00:28:55.295 --> 00:28:56.428
Dying stuff.


00:28:57.063 --> 00:28:58.097
Just be you...


00:28:59.466 --> 00:29:00.766
Daniel.


00:29:03.103 --> 00:29:04.803
With all your Daniel junk.


00:29:06.473 --> 00:29:07.506
Come on.


00:29:09.209 --> 00:29:10.242
Let's go.


00:29:45.211 --> 00:29:46.245
Hmm.


00:29:48.348 --> 00:29:52.985
Was kind of hoping that you guys
would have the upgraded side.


00:29:54.320 --> 00:29:56.789
Maybe a tempur-pedic chair...


00:29:58.057 --> 00:29:59.914
Flat-screen.


00:29:59.994 --> 00:30:02.149
Would it kill you to get
some reading material in here?


00:30:02.229 --> 00:30:04.329
This was a mistake.
No, it isn't.


00:30:05.832 --> 00:30:06.865
Relax.


00:30:08.234 --> 00:30:09.301
Relax.


00:30:11.171 --> 00:30:13.172
You don't look relaxed.
Relax. Breathe.


00:30:16.309 --> 00:30:17.476
Good job.


00:30:18.211 --> 00:30:19.244
So?


00:30:21.381 --> 00:30:22.414
So?


00:30:24.117 --> 00:30:25.906
You're gonna make me explain


00:30:25.986 --> 00:30:28.053
this process to you? No,
I just... I don't...


00:30:31.291 --> 00:30:33.292
Now, Daniel.
Hmm.


00:30:34.194 --> 00:30:36.083
My child.
Mm-hmm.


00:30:36.163 --> 00:30:37.985
My lamb.


00:30:38.065 --> 00:30:39.431
My lambchop child.


00:30:42.101 --> 00:30:43.335
Unburden yourself.


00:30:45.438 --> 00:30:46.538
Get absolved.


00:30:48.541 --> 00:30:49.541
Speak.


00:30:50.476 --> 00:30:51.844
Whatever you want to say.


00:31:08.061 --> 00:31:09.127
I don't see.


00:31:10.163 --> 00:31:11.563
You don't see?


00:31:14.267 --> 00:31:15.300
No.


00:31:16.502 --> 00:31:18.971
You don't see what?


00:31:25.044 --> 00:31:26.078
God.


00:31:28.414 --> 00:31:30.449
God... what?


00:31:38.458 --> 00:31:40.392
I don't see god.


00:31:49.235 --> 00:31:51.036
I don't think I ever have.


00:31:59.612 --> 00:32:01.013
My, uh...


00:32:06.252 --> 00:32:07.586
My dad died...


00:32:09.389 --> 00:32:11.156
Last year, and, uh...


00:32:14.327 --> 00:32:17.462
He always liked the idea
of having a priest as a son.


00:32:18.698 --> 00:32:20.621
I mean, I liked the idea, too.
Don't get me wrong.


00:32:20.701 --> 00:32:22.923
It wasn't like he forced me
into it or anything.


00:32:23.003 --> 00:32:24.036
It was just...


00:32:26.472 --> 00:32:27.940
Just made sense.


00:32:28.942 --> 00:32:29.942
You know?


00:32:32.312 --> 00:32:34.268
Some kids want to grow up and...


00:32:34.348 --> 00:32:37.215
Pitch game seven
at Yankee stadium...


00:32:38.051 --> 00:32:39.607
Give an Oscar speech...


00:32:39.687 --> 00:32:43.088
Fight fires or terrorists or...


00:32:43.690 --> 00:32:45.279
Whatever.


00:32:45.359 --> 00:32:48.226
I wanted to wear the fancy robes
on Sundays...


00:32:49.729 --> 00:32:52.998
Give homilies
to captive audiences every week.


00:33:00.039 --> 00:33:02.207
Help people.


00:33:18.524 --> 00:33:20.525
He never missed a single mass.


00:33:23.329 --> 00:33:24.629
Even when he got sick.


00:33:34.307 --> 00:33:36.308
He used to tell people that...


00:33:38.077 --> 00:33:40.278
He wasn't afraid of death
because...


00:33:43.049 --> 00:33:45.183
My Danny's got it in with
the big guy.


00:33:51.491 --> 00:33:53.692
Truth is
he was never worried though.


00:33:55.762 --> 00:33:57.329
He saw him every day.


00:34:00.233 --> 00:34:01.333
But you don't.


00:34:01.667 --> 00:34:02.701
No.


00:34:05.338 --> 00:34:07.205
So why do you do this?


00:34:15.181 --> 00:34:18.750
Because if god ever does
show up, I...


00:34:22.088 --> 00:34:23.321
I don't want to miss it.


00:34:35.835 --> 00:34:38.993
I was sort of hoping for impure
thoughts about the organ lady.


00:34:39.073 --> 00:34:40.561
Um...


00:34:40.641 --> 00:34:41.673
But...


00:34:42.575 --> 00:34:43.675
This'll do.


00:34:48.381 --> 00:34:49.448
So what now?


00:34:52.351 --> 00:34:56.243
Uh, well... I guess
you could give me a penance.


00:34:56.323 --> 00:34:57.522
Really?
Yeah.


00:34:58.257 --> 00:34:59.458
Nice.


00:34:59.859 --> 00:35:01.293
Um...


00:35:02.328 --> 00:35:03.795
Five hail Marys,


00:35:04.797 --> 00:35:07.699
three our fathers...


00:35:09.168 --> 00:35:10.402
Two...


00:35:13.406 --> 00:35:15.295
Twenty pushups.


00:35:15.375 --> 00:35:18.577
And you have to come
to my show next weekend.


00:35:18.878 --> 00:35:20.067
Show?


00:35:20.147 --> 00:35:22.603
I'm huge in this town.


00:35:22.683 --> 00:35:25.372
I'm surprised you're not already
familiar with my music,


00:35:25.452 --> 00:35:27.408
but I guess
this'll give you a chance


00:35:27.488 --> 00:35:30.110
to get hip to what the kids
are into these days.


00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:32.146
Um, I don't...
Oh, you're totally coming.


00:35:32.226 --> 00:35:34.181
I'll save you a seat up front.


00:35:34.261 --> 00:35:36.717
I can comp you, but you gotta
buy some coffee or something,


00:35:36.797 --> 00:35:40.054
or the owner's gonna get pissy. Okay?
I really don't think this...


00:35:40.134 --> 00:35:44.324
Great. I'll give you the details
at our next confession slash date.


00:35:44.404 --> 00:35:48.128
Jane. Jane.
Jane!


00:35:48.208 --> 00:35:51.098
Yes, you can buy merch from me
directly after the show.


00:35:51.178 --> 00:35:52.766
Jane, I...
Autographs are fine,


00:35:52.846 --> 00:35:55.247
but, please, no photos.


00:36:21.374 --> 00:36:22.807
Miss your run again?


00:36:27.480 --> 00:36:28.402
Want a muffin?


00:36:28.482 --> 00:36:31.371
They're minis, so...
You can have, like,


00:36:31.451 --> 00:36:33.518
Thirty of them, and they're
still not that bad for you.


00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:39.391
Why do you do this?


00:36:44.964 --> 00:36:46.653
I'm addicted to refined sugar.


00:36:46.733 --> 00:36:49.289
It just tastes so darn good
on everything,


00:36:49.369 --> 00:36:51.758
and if that's a sin, I just figure
I'll work it out on the other side,


00:36:51.838 --> 00:36:53.538
but Adam had his apple, and I...


00:36:54.473 --> 00:36:56.296
Truth be told,


00:36:56.376 --> 00:36:58.799
I'm just looking for one
guilt-free sleeve of oreos,


00:36:58.879 --> 00:37:00.612
and I don't think that's
too much to ask.


00:37:02.648 --> 00:37:04.749
That's not what I meant.
I know.


00:37:08.454 --> 00:37:09.776
So what...


00:37:09.856 --> 00:37:11.223
What's going on with you?


00:37:12.358 --> 00:37:13.680
I don't know.


00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:16.750
But you're hoping
I can offer you


00:37:16.830 --> 00:37:19.386
some sort of divine nugget
of wisdom


00:37:19.466 --> 00:37:22.000
that'll make all the pieces
add up together for you?


00:37:22.768 --> 00:37:23.924
What's the story?


00:37:24.004 --> 00:37:26.760
Having a crisis of faith or...


00:37:26.840 --> 00:37:28.162
Something else?


00:37:28.242 --> 00:37:29.307
I have faith.


00:37:32.279 --> 00:37:36.548
Yippee! Good for you,
father Jamieson.


00:37:36.816 --> 00:37:37.838
I just...


00:37:37.918 --> 00:37:38.950
I mean, I'm...


00:37:40.353 --> 00:37:41.742
I'm just trying to
figure it out,


00:37:41.822 --> 00:37:42.988
and you...


00:37:44.991 --> 00:37:46.280
Forget it.


00:37:46.360 --> 00:37:47.440
Did you do the last rights?


00:37:47.793 --> 00:37:48.827
What?


00:37:52.031 --> 00:37:53.365
When your dad died.


00:37:55.434 --> 00:37:57.257
Were you the one
who gave him his last rights?


00:37:57.337 --> 00:37:58.470
Yes.


00:37:59.805 --> 00:38:01.406
And how did that feel?


00:38:04.043 --> 00:38:05.644
He told me it was worth it...


00:38:06.746 --> 00:38:07.801
Dying...


00:38:07.881 --> 00:38:11.583
In order for me to be
the one to anoint him.


00:38:13.352 --> 00:38:14.486
What about you, though?


00:38:17.890 --> 00:38:19.024
How did you feel?


00:38:20.826 --> 00:38:23.395
Gracious?
Did you feel...


00:38:24.330 --> 00:38:25.397
Blessed?


00:38:29.468 --> 00:38:30.568
Just sad.


00:38:37.310 --> 00:38:38.743
Go ahead and have a seat,
will ya?


00:38:43.816 --> 00:38:45.383
Go ahead and take the whole box.


00:38:47.653 --> 00:38:48.887
Yeah, they're gluten free.


00:38:49.655 --> 00:38:50.789
Organic.


00:38:54.026 --> 00:38:55.406
Mostly locally sourced.


00:38:58.030 --> 00:39:01.355
Not quite farm to table, but...


00:39:01.435 --> 00:39:03.968
pretty good.


00:39:12.478 --> 00:39:14.735
So I've got
the second Sunday mass,


00:39:14.815 --> 00:39:17.037
a baptism on Saturday afternoon,


00:39:17.117 --> 00:39:19.406
and the Monday-morning
confession.


00:39:19.486 --> 00:39:20.907
Wednesday choir practice


00:39:20.987 --> 00:39:22.809
and the Saturday-evening mass.


00:39:22.889 --> 00:39:25.012
Oh, and this is pretty fun:


00:39:25.092 --> 00:39:27.826
The kids from Sunday school
have asked me to...


00:39:28.728 --> 00:39:29.961
To come in and teach a lesson.


00:39:31.130 --> 00:39:32.364
You?


00:39:32.665 --> 00:39:33.798
Yeah.


00:39:34.433 --> 00:39:35.856
It's strange.


00:39:35.936 --> 00:39:37.524
It turns out that
they find some people


00:39:37.604 --> 00:39:40.661
a little more relatable
than others.


00:39:40.741 --> 00:39:42.774
Well, they're only
eight years old, so...


00:39:44.745 --> 00:39:46.500
And I will be spending quite
a bit of time


00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:47.668
over at Ronnie's.


00:39:47.748 --> 00:39:49.069
Why not the hospital?


00:39:49.149 --> 00:39:51.305
No, that stubborn
son of a bitch,


00:39:51.385 --> 00:39:52.517
he just refuses to...


00:39:53.819 --> 00:39:55.676
Let go.


00:39:55.756 --> 00:39:58.945
They have moved him home.
He is strictly hospice now.


00:39:59.025 --> 00:40:01.048
He's really still alive?


00:40:01.128 --> 00:40:03.383
Well, I'll tell you what,
father.


00:40:03.463 --> 00:40:06.019
I will let him know that his
selfish need to cling to life


00:40:06.099 --> 00:40:08.422
is disrupting his schedule.
How's that sound?


00:40:08.502 --> 00:40:10.891
Hmm. How's your week looking?


00:40:10.971 --> 00:40:12.793
It's pretty much
the same as the last,


00:40:12.873 --> 00:40:14.828
except for a few adjustments.


00:40:14.908 --> 00:40:16.730
Uh, n-not so fast.


00:40:16.810 --> 00:40:19.933
You'll be happy to know that
I talked to the bishop,


00:40:20.013 --> 00:40:24.338
and he agreed to drop
the Friday night confessions.


00:40:24.418 --> 00:40:28.008
I... it... I just think
that maybe we should...


00:40:28.088 --> 00:40:31.478
Well, the church
is going back to normal hours.


00:40:31.558 --> 00:40:33.491
Building will close at night.


00:40:34.026 --> 00:40:35.493
End of story.


00:40:36.061 --> 00:40:37.095
Okay?


00:40:37.596 --> 00:40:38.630
Okay.


00:40:46.906 --> 00:40:49.529
<i>No, mom, they don't
call mourning "morning"</i>


00:40:49.609 --> 00:40:51.031
<i>because it's supposed to happen
every day.</i>


00:40:51.111 --> 00:40:52.544
<i>Who told you that?</i>


00:40:56.482 --> 00:40:57.515
<i>I know.</i>


00:40:58.884 --> 00:40:59.918
<i>I know.</i>


00:41:02.521 --> 00:41:03.988
<i>But I don't let it take over.</i>


00:41:04.990 --> 00:41:06.858
<i>He wouldn't have wanted us to...</i>


00:41:09.028 --> 00:41:11.095
<i>Everything happens for a reason.</i>


00:41:15.134 --> 00:41:16.601
<i>I love you too, mom.</i>


00:41:17.970 --> 00:41:19.037
<i>God bless.</i>


00:43:44.984 --> 00:43:46.673
Problem was
I couldn't sing Harmony,


00:43:46.753 --> 00:43:49.242
and the other problem was
I couldn't sing melody.


00:43:49.322 --> 00:43:51.122
So...
This is me.


00:43:52.324 --> 00:43:54.981
Oh... nice.


00:43:55.061 --> 00:43:57.050
Place.
Weird, right?


00:43:57.130 --> 00:43:58.184
Hmm?


00:43:58.264 --> 00:43:59.931
I actually live somewhere.


00:44:01.333 --> 00:44:02.934
Now I'm real, too.


00:44:04.670 --> 00:44:05.959
Thanks for walking me home.


00:44:06.039 --> 00:44:08.039
I always wanted a priest
as a bodyguard.


00:44:08.874 --> 00:44:09.863
You don't really strike me


00:44:09.943 --> 00:44:10.931
as the type of person


00:44:11.011 --> 00:44:11.965
that needs protection.


00:44:12.045 --> 00:44:13.277
We all need it, Daniel.


00:44:14.046 --> 00:44:16.036
The world kinda sucks.


00:44:16.116 --> 00:44:16.970
You don't believe that.


00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:18.004
No, you don't,


00:44:18.084 --> 00:44:19.105
which is why I like you,


00:44:19.185 --> 00:44:21.019
but you're also, you know...


00:44:21.887 --> 00:44:22.920
You.


00:44:24.723 --> 00:44:26.646
Again, confirming my world view.


00:44:26.726 --> 00:44:29.115
What's that supposed to mean?
Oh, nothing.


00:44:29.195 --> 00:44:32.686
Nothing here.
Just a lovely friendship.


00:44:32.766 --> 00:44:33.753
What's wrong with that?


00:44:33.833 --> 00:44:35.055
Nothing.


00:44:35.135 --> 00:44:37.201
You're a priest.
I'm dying.


00:44:38.103 --> 00:44:39.192
I get it,


00:44:39.272 --> 00:44:41.328
but in different circumstances,


00:44:41.408 --> 00:44:44.409
we're totally dating right now.
No. No, I...


00:44:45.844 --> 00:44:48.101
No.
Wow, father,


00:44:48.181 --> 00:44:50.303
you really know
how to make a girl feel special.


00:44:50.383 --> 00:44:52.105
No, I mean...


00:44:52.185 --> 00:44:53.640
This isn't...


00:44:53.720 --> 00:44:55.609
I-I... we're...


00:44:55.689 --> 00:44:56.943
I... I wouldn't say that...


00:44:57.023 --> 00:44:58.345
That... I mean, we're not.


00:44:58.425 --> 00:45:00.313
I-I'm not. You know?


00:45:00.393 --> 00:45:01.815
No, I don't,


00:45:01.895 --> 00:45:03.817
but I'd be happy
to give feedback


00:45:03.897 --> 00:45:06.019
if you feel compelled
to articulate


00:45:06.099 --> 00:45:07.465
an entire thought.


00:45:14.873 --> 00:45:17.108
I am committed to god.


00:45:18.844 --> 00:45:20.845
That means that any...


00:45:21.880 --> 00:45:25.116
Emotional connection,


00:45:25.484 --> 00:45:26.873
that is...


00:45:26.953 --> 00:45:28.742
Other than friendship,


00:45:28.822 --> 00:45:30.910
which... which is
what I think that we have...


00:45:30.990 --> 00:45:32.145
Friendship.


00:45:32.225 --> 00:45:34.058
You know? A really strong...


00:45:35.027 --> 00:45:37.651
But anything more than that


00:45:37.731 --> 00:45:40.754
is obviously not allowed.


00:45:40.834 --> 00:45:42.355
I mean,
it goes against everything...


00:45:42.435 --> 00:45:44.335
Uh... everything...


00:45:46.939 --> 00:45:48.406
That I am, so...


00:45:50.976 --> 00:45:53.778
How do you expect to get laid if you
keep saying that kind of stuff?


00:45:57.149 --> 00:45:59.016
That was a joke. Relax.


00:46:01.887 --> 00:46:04.911
Well, you're probably going
to hell because of it,


00:46:04.991 --> 00:46:06.924
so I really hope
it was worth it.


00:46:12.231 --> 00:46:14.132
I really can't tell jokes,
can I?


00:46:16.802 --> 00:46:17.835
Come on!


00:46:18.537 --> 00:46:19.904
No, man, sorry.


00:46:22.174 --> 00:46:24.397
But you did really sell
the whole humorless,


00:46:24.477 --> 00:46:26.332
stodgy priest thing there.
Yeah.


00:46:26.412 --> 00:46:29.280
We work on it in seminary,
for years.


00:46:30.249 --> 00:46:31.849
Yeah,
that and thurible swinging.


00:46:32.518 --> 00:46:34.152
Thurible swinging?
Yeah.


00:46:35.320 --> 00:46:36.554
Sounds dirty.


00:46:38.290 --> 00:46:39.791
Uh, well...


00:46:40.392 --> 00:46:42.415
Sorry. It's late.


00:46:42.495 --> 00:46:43.795
You're cute.


00:46:44.563 --> 00:46:46.086
I'm human.


00:46:46.166 --> 00:46:49.089
Can I... ask you a question?


00:46:49.169 --> 00:46:50.201
Maybe.


00:46:52.404 --> 00:46:53.259
The whole dying thing.


00:46:53.339 --> 00:46:54.961
No.
What?


00:46:55.041 --> 00:46:56.863
Let's not.
Come on.


00:46:56.943 --> 00:46:59.432
You've got off-limits,
you know, stuff. So do I.


00:46:59.512 --> 00:47:02.102
Well, we both know that
you're not... Daniel.


00:47:02.182 --> 00:47:03.915
I mean,
you don't even look sick.


00:47:04.550 --> 00:47:05.917
Like at all.


00:47:08.387 --> 00:47:10.143
It's late.
I should go inside.


00:47:10.223 --> 00:47:11.389
Jane.


00:47:12.391 --> 00:47:13.858
Thanks for walking me home.


00:47:14.526 --> 00:47:16.327
I didn't mean to...


00:47:17.095 --> 00:47:18.162
It's just...


00:47:19.998 --> 00:47:23.957
I don't know why we have to keep
up with the, you know, charade.


00:47:24.037 --> 00:47:25.358
Charade?


00:47:25.438 --> 00:47:26.860
No, that's not what I...


00:47:26.940 --> 00:47:28.039
I-I just mean...


00:47:28.574 --> 00:47:30.374
You don't...


00:47:31.210 --> 00:47:32.877
I mean, you look...
How?


00:47:33.178 --> 00:47:34.212
What?


00:47:37.482 --> 00:47:38.583
How do I look?


00:47:40.252 --> 00:47:42.587
Well, no, I just...


00:47:45.157 --> 00:47:46.524
I don't look frail...


00:47:48.360 --> 00:47:49.393
Helpless?


00:47:55.934 --> 00:47:57.568
I seem a bit too healthy?


00:47:59.238 --> 00:48:04.876
Well, I guess that's a testament
to my formidable spirit.


00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:11.315
Good night, friend.


00:48:53.326 --> 00:48:55.326
There's a decent case
for blasphemy here...


00:49:07.340 --> 00:49:11.598
You see? Keep missing
your morning jogs,


00:49:11.678 --> 00:49:13.511
breaking your routine,


00:49:14.279 --> 00:49:15.346
that's your future.


00:49:22.321 --> 00:49:23.354
What?


00:49:24.089 --> 00:49:25.122
Nothing.


00:49:26.291 --> 00:49:27.347
Daniel, say it.


00:49:27.427 --> 00:49:30.083
He's happy.
What?


00:49:30.163 --> 00:49:34.231
I know that you take some issue with
father Ollie's eccentricities, but...


00:49:35.467 --> 00:49:37.101
He treats this like a joke.


00:49:37.502 --> 00:49:39.036
But look at him.


00:50:01.260 --> 00:50:03.049
That's what I'm talking about.


00:50:03.129 --> 00:50:05.018
Good, good, good, good, good.


00:50:05.098 --> 00:50:07.186
Lost your snare
at the bridge, keyshawn...


00:50:07.266 --> 00:50:09.667
He's wearing basketball shoes.


00:50:10.268 --> 00:50:11.257
Under his habit.


00:50:11.337 --> 00:50:12.525
You know what I mean.


00:50:12.605 --> 00:50:15.172
I'm not so sure... actually.


00:50:17.609 --> 00:50:18.642
Never mind.


00:50:19.077 --> 00:50:20.244
Doug?


00:50:22.347 --> 00:50:23.581
Were you lip syncing?


00:50:24.416 --> 00:50:26.083
No.
Doug.


00:50:27.052 --> 00:50:28.285
No.
Doug.


00:50:32.224 --> 00:50:33.424
And I broke Doug.


00:50:34.092 --> 00:50:35.192
That's on me.


00:50:35.560 --> 00:50:36.582
That's my bad.


00:50:36.662 --> 00:50:40.320
Daniel... I should probably
go get some work done.


00:50:40.400 --> 00:50:41.454
Doug, come.
Sit.


00:50:41.534 --> 00:50:44.223
Come here. Come here.
Come here.


00:50:44.303 --> 00:50:45.625
C'mere, c'mere, c'mere...


00:50:45.705 --> 00:50:47.805
Doug, sing these...


00:50:52.811 --> 00:50:54.245
Bring your air down lower.


00:51:01.087 --> 00:51:03.977
And you're back.
I'm so proud of you.


00:51:04.057 --> 00:51:06.290
That's the way to...
What's going on here?


00:51:07.759 --> 00:51:09.048
What is it?


00:51:09.128 --> 00:51:10.294
I met someone.


00:51:10.695 --> 00:51:12.163
You met someone?


00:51:12.564 --> 00:51:13.664
Yes.


00:51:16.234 --> 00:51:17.490
What does that mean?


00:51:17.570 --> 00:51:19.625
A person.
I met a person.


00:51:19.705 --> 00:51:21.539
There was a person,
and I met her.


00:51:22.641 --> 00:51:23.674
Her?


00:51:24.376 --> 00:51:25.409
Yes.


00:51:28.246 --> 00:51:29.280
Hmm.


00:51:30.348 --> 00:51:31.382
I see.


00:51:32.551 --> 00:51:33.573
No big deal.


00:51:33.653 --> 00:51:35.375
And that's what happens


00:51:35.455 --> 00:51:37.421
when you apply
a little bit of enthusiasm...


00:51:40.426 --> 00:51:41.592
Doug!


00:51:42.828 --> 00:51:45.118
Now you're embarrassing yourself


00:51:45.198 --> 00:51:46.597
in a place of worship.


00:51:47.199 --> 00:51:49.022
Take a knee.


00:51:49.102 --> 00:51:51.657
You will not be in this
rehearsal until I tell you.


00:51:51.737 --> 00:51:55.061
So it wasn't
just someone you met.


00:51:55.141 --> 00:51:57.741
You... you met her.


00:51:58.543 --> 00:52:01.567
A... female someone.


00:52:01.647 --> 00:52:03.347
I didn't do anything, father.


00:52:03.882 --> 00:52:05.171
No one says you did.


00:52:05.251 --> 00:52:07.273
Because I didn't.
Okay.


00:52:07.353 --> 00:52:09.509
So it doesn't matter if it was
a female someone or a her


00:52:09.589 --> 00:52:13.324
if I didn't do anything, which I
didn't, so it doesn't... matter.


00:52:13.859 --> 00:52:15.359
Great.
Terrific.


00:52:16.161 --> 00:52:17.228
Glory be.


00:52:28.540 --> 00:52:30.274
I didn't do anything, father.


00:52:32.911 --> 00:52:36.836
Well, that's between you
and god, now, isn't it?


00:52:36.916 --> 00:52:38.671
Let's go one more time.
Let's feel it.


00:52:38.751 --> 00:52:41.385
Practice makes perfect.


00:53:13.919 --> 00:53:15.586
B-4.


00:53:18.723 --> 00:53:21.225
Bingo Thursdays with
Edith and Ruth.


00:53:22.360 --> 00:53:23.316
And Jane.


00:53:23.396 --> 00:53:24.828
<i>G-51.</i>


00:53:25.397 --> 00:53:26.797
Oh! G-51.


00:53:31.303 --> 00:53:33.237
When you're blessed,
you're blessed. Am I right?


00:53:34.839 --> 00:53:35.873
Yeah?


00:53:36.841 --> 00:53:37.875
No?


00:53:40.212 --> 00:53:41.367
Okay.


00:53:41.447 --> 00:53:42.980
<i>I-17.</i>


00:53:46.451 --> 00:53:48.719
Nope. No I-17.


00:53:49.387 --> 00:53:50.510
I-16.


00:53:50.590 --> 00:53:52.690
I-18 would've done it.
But no.


00:53:56.795 --> 00:53:59.930
This is fun. Let me know
when you really wanna talk.


00:54:02.400 --> 00:54:03.322
Jane.


00:54:03.402 --> 00:54:04.735
<i>E-7.</i>


00:54:07.772 --> 00:54:08.939
I got you something.


00:54:10.575 --> 00:54:12.543
What is it?
Open it.


00:54:13.411 --> 00:54:14.912
I wasn't expecting you'd...


00:54:16.715 --> 00:54:19.372
You've been holding out on me.


00:54:19.452 --> 00:54:21.785
I don't know what to say.


00:54:23.488 --> 00:54:27.424
I'm pleasantly... surprised.


00:54:29.761 --> 00:54:31.284
Is this a joke?


00:54:31.364 --> 00:54:33.998
What do you mean?
I don't understand.


00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:36.867
<i>E-46.</i>


00:54:40.538 --> 00:54:43.796
Don't do this Daniel.
Please.


00:54:43.876 --> 00:54:47.578
You of all people. I'm not letting you
turn out to be a disappointment too.


00:54:49.581 --> 00:54:50.914
<i>O-68.</i>


00:54:53.485 --> 00:54:56.509
Please, just... take that.


00:54:56.589 --> 00:54:57.721
For your sake.


00:55:00.492 --> 00:55:01.592
For my sake?


00:55:02.494 --> 00:55:03.560
See you around.


00:55:03.895 --> 00:55:05.062
Father.


00:55:07.832 --> 00:55:09.733
<i>I-43.</i>


00:55:11.069 --> 00:55:12.469
Where are we?


00:55:15.307 --> 00:55:16.696
Why are we here?


00:55:16.776 --> 00:55:19.398
No, no no, don't.
Don't try to answer.


00:55:19.478 --> 00:55:22.012
Just maybe give that some
thought for a second or two.


00:55:24.849 --> 00:55:26.505
Why are we here?


00:55:26.585 --> 00:55:28.374
I mean, I can tell you
for a fact


00:55:28.454 --> 00:55:31.010
I'm only here
for the free communion wafers.


00:55:31.090 --> 00:55:33.057
'Course that's just me.
But the rest of you.


00:55:34.459 --> 00:55:35.492
Why?


00:55:36.861 --> 00:55:41.654
And I, I don't mean
philosophically.


00:55:41.734 --> 00:55:45.658
I mean right now.
In this exact moment.


00:55:45.738 --> 00:55:48.439
What brought you into
this building?


00:55:49.040 --> 00:55:50.429
Guilt?


00:55:50.509 --> 00:55:53.266
Fear? Obligation?


00:55:53.346 --> 00:55:56.769
Perhaps you aren't
even into the big radio hits.


00:55:56.849 --> 00:55:59.639
And you're more of a deep track,
b-side kind of guy.


00:55:59.719 --> 00:56:03.887
So, are you looking for
a sense of community?


00:56:04.989 --> 00:56:06.790
A moment of reflection?


00:56:08.593 --> 00:56:09.793
An escape?


00:56:12.130 --> 00:56:13.686
You can do a lot worse.


00:56:13.766 --> 00:56:18.502
This really is
a beautiful building.


00:56:19.537 --> 00:56:21.438
Oh my goodness.


00:56:22.807 --> 00:56:23.841
But...


00:56:24.409 --> 00:56:25.409
But...


00:56:26.144 --> 00:56:28.034
If what brought you here


00:56:28.114 --> 00:56:33.150
doesn't at least have something
to do with compassion.


00:56:35.086 --> 00:56:36.742
Well then, that's all there
really is.


00:56:36.822 --> 00:56:37.855
Huh?


00:56:39.457 --> 00:56:40.491
A building.


00:56:43.528 --> 00:56:44.561
Compassion.


00:56:45.163 --> 00:56:46.852
Oh, what a concept.


00:56:46.932 --> 00:56:50.022
I mean, we all like to think
that we are...


00:56:50.102 --> 00:56:51.624
Compassionate.


00:56:51.704 --> 00:56:53.426
Help you feel better.


00:56:53.506 --> 00:56:56.540
Thoughts and prayers.
I'm so very sorry for your loss.


00:56:59.110 --> 00:57:01.512
But it's a funny thing though.


00:57:03.448 --> 00:57:07.451
Because when you find out where the word
compassion comes from, it's real...


00:57:07.819 --> 00:57:08.741
Origin.


00:57:08.821 --> 00:57:11.855
It turns out
the word actually means


00:57:14.058 --> 00:57:15.592
to suffer with.


00:57:15.994 --> 00:57:17.483
Not to pity.


00:57:17.563 --> 00:57:19.618
Not to feel sorry for,


00:57:19.698 --> 00:57:23.133
not to send hugs
to somebody's Facebook wall.


00:57:25.170 --> 00:57:26.770
But to suffer with.


00:57:29.774 --> 00:57:31.397
And are you capable


00:57:31.477 --> 00:57:32.943
of suffering with


00:57:34.179 --> 00:57:35.546
someone else?


00:57:36.548 --> 00:57:37.748
To...


00:57:39.984 --> 00:57:41.718
Take on their pain.


00:57:43.555 --> 00:57:45.756
And carry it around with you
for a while.


00:57:48.493 --> 00:57:49.626
Someone...


00:57:52.831 --> 00:57:53.931
Hurting.


00:57:55.099 --> 00:57:56.200
Someone...


00:57:59.804 --> 00:58:01.071
Completely lost.


00:58:02.640 --> 00:58:03.674
Someone...


00:58:05.577 --> 00:58:07.099
With less than you.


00:58:07.179 --> 00:58:09.168
Less money.


00:58:09.248 --> 00:58:12.516
Less stuff. Yeah, whatever.
But what about less freedom?


00:58:14.652 --> 00:58:15.641
Less choice.


00:58:15.721 --> 00:58:16.753
Less...


00:58:17.856 --> 00:58:18.889
Privilege.


00:58:21.125 --> 00:58:22.926
Less basic human rights.


00:58:27.966 --> 00:58:30.100
Are you truly able to
suffer with...


00:58:33.037 --> 00:58:34.137
Others?


00:58:37.041 --> 00:58:38.175
But,


00:58:40.945 --> 00:58:41.979
will you?


00:58:48.286 --> 00:58:49.653
How much I owe you?


00:58:57.829 --> 00:59:00.297
Good run? Good, good, yeah.
Very good.


00:59:00.932 --> 00:59:01.965
Very focused.


00:59:02.600 --> 00:59:03.622
Good.


00:59:03.702 --> 00:59:05.090
It was great, actually.


00:59:05.170 --> 00:59:06.459
It was,


00:59:06.539 --> 00:59:08.894
it was great.
Great.


00:59:08.974 --> 00:59:11.030
I would definitely classify that
run as great.


00:59:11.110 --> 00:59:13.610
If I were to classify it.
Which apparently I am. So...


00:59:14.779 --> 00:59:18.115
Yep. I would file it
under g for great.


00:59:23.621 --> 00:59:24.621
How's scripture?


00:59:24.989 --> 00:59:25.945
Wonderful.


00:59:26.025 --> 00:59:26.946
It is.


00:59:27.026 --> 00:59:29.626
Always wonderful. Scripture.


00:59:35.600 --> 00:59:38.635
I'm just going to go ahead and
opt out of this conversation.


00:59:48.313 --> 00:59:49.813
How's it going?


00:59:52.650 --> 00:59:53.850
'Kay, I'm on my way.


00:59:54.819 --> 00:59:55.975
Everything okay?


00:59:56.055 --> 00:59:57.843
It's Ronnie.
He's on his way out.


00:59:57.923 --> 00:59:59.512
Well, perhaps you should allow
the family to...


00:59:59.592 --> 01:00:00.880
He asked for me.


01:00:00.960 --> 01:00:02.047
Oh. You've spent so much time...


01:00:02.127 --> 01:00:03.961
He asked for me, Victor.


01:00:06.998 --> 01:00:08.621
Of course.


01:00:08.701 --> 01:00:10.022
If one of you could cover


01:00:10.102 --> 01:00:11.690
my 10:00am confession,
that'd be Ter...


01:00:11.770 --> 01:00:13.859
- Can I go with you?
- No.


01:00:13.939 --> 01:00:16.640
- What if, uh...
- We'll finish in the car.


01:01:57.408 --> 01:01:59.042
So, dying sucks.


01:02:02.013 --> 01:02:02.935
You okay?


01:02:03.015 --> 01:02:06.405
Yeah. I didn't
really know him, so...


01:02:06.485 --> 01:02:07.984
Well, that's not what I asked.


01:02:10.488 --> 01:02:11.955
I'm fine.


01:02:16.360 --> 01:02:18.128
It's awfully easy
to forget, but,


01:02:20.965 --> 01:02:24.334
we're pretty damn lucky to
be able to do what we do.


01:02:26.070 --> 01:02:27.170
Priests?


01:02:30.007 --> 01:02:31.041
Humans.


01:02:35.447 --> 01:02:37.269
What'd you say?


01:02:37.349 --> 01:02:39.216
Wanna crush a little Arby's
on the way home?


01:02:49.428 --> 01:02:50.428
Thank you.


01:02:51.362 --> 01:02:52.785
You know, it's fans like you


01:02:52.865 --> 01:02:54.397
that really make it all
worth-while.


01:02:56.100 --> 01:02:57.389
You see, that was actually funny


01:02:57.469 --> 01:02:59.758
because you guys
aren't being supportive


01:02:59.838 --> 01:03:00.959
at all.


01:03:01.039 --> 01:03:02.139
Is why it's funny.


01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:03.907
What I just said.


01:03:07.044 --> 01:03:08.044
Okay.


01:03:14.553 --> 01:03:16.942
I cheered.


01:03:17.022 --> 01:03:18.911
Probably couldn't hear me because
I was standing outside the door.


01:03:18.991 --> 01:03:20.023
What do you want?


01:03:20.558 --> 01:03:22.047
I'm sorry.
For what?


01:03:22.127 --> 01:03:24.149
For the other day and the Bible.


01:03:24.229 --> 01:03:25.784
Just say being a dick.


01:03:25.864 --> 01:03:27.953
What?
I'm sorry for being a dick.


01:03:28.033 --> 01:03:29.432
That should cover everything.


01:03:32.203 --> 01:03:34.727
I'm sorry for... yes, Daniel,
you can take me home.


01:03:34.807 --> 01:03:36.261
But please no funny business.


01:03:36.341 --> 01:03:38.809
I'm saving myself for
the right clergyman.


01:03:47.819 --> 01:03:48.985
You want something to drink?


01:03:49.554 --> 01:03:50.587
Uh, yeah.


01:03:51.255 --> 01:03:53.345
I have...


01:03:53.425 --> 01:03:57.027
Water. And... water.


01:03:57.995 --> 01:03:59.029
And...


01:03:59.831 --> 01:04:00.864
Well, water.


01:04:02.033 --> 01:04:03.600
Water would be great.


01:04:04.235 --> 01:04:05.302
Great.


01:04:06.470 --> 01:04:08.071
Make yourself at home.


01:04:39.971 --> 01:04:41.638
It's amazing. Isn't it?


01:04:45.376 --> 01:04:46.565
Jane.


01:04:46.645 --> 01:04:48.300
No.
What?


01:04:48.380 --> 01:04:50.569
You said Jane like, Jane.


01:04:50.649 --> 01:04:52.037
What does that mean?


01:04:52.117 --> 01:04:53.839
That tone.
I had a tone?


01:04:53.919 --> 01:04:55.307
Um, yeah. That, you know...


01:04:55.387 --> 01:04:58.021
Eat your vegetables tone.
Jane.


01:04:58.623 --> 01:04:59.912
Don't do it.


01:04:59.992 --> 01:05:01.246
I, can we just...
Don't.


01:05:01.326 --> 01:05:03.348
I just wanna ask...
We had a good thing.


01:05:03.428 --> 01:05:05.017
Why would you wanna mess that...


01:05:05.097 --> 01:05:06.852
Do you even know
what it is that I'm gonna ask?


01:05:06.932 --> 01:05:08.020
Yeah.
Really?


01:05:08.100 --> 01:05:09.421
Yeah.
So?


01:05:09.501 --> 01:05:12.157
So, what?
Eh-tell me.


01:05:12.237 --> 01:05:15.594
Why would I say something out loud that
I'm practically begging you not to ask?


01:05:15.674 --> 01:05:18.197
Because you realize that
I'm asking you a real question.


01:05:18.277 --> 01:05:21.244
You miss, uh, I-sing.


01:05:22.079 --> 01:05:24.503
And-I'm-emotionally-fearless.


01:05:24.583 --> 01:05:27.139
And-i-do-really-
weird-things-to-my-hair.


01:05:27.219 --> 01:05:30.520
To-try-and-make-it-less-attractive-but-it-always-
makes-it-more-attractive.


01:05:34.425 --> 01:05:37.661
You're afraid to let somebody
know who you are.


01:05:43.034 --> 01:05:45.135
You think this makes me
more attractive? Okay.


01:05:53.377 --> 01:05:56.579
You were going to ask me about
the whole death thing. Again.


01:05:59.984 --> 01:06:01.151
I told you I knew.


01:06:04.388 --> 01:06:05.655
Do you get that a lot?


01:06:06.223 --> 01:06:07.257
Yeah.


01:06:09.527 --> 01:06:11.494
Right before
I never see someone again.


01:06:21.672 --> 01:06:23.028
I'm not going anywhere.


01:06:23.108 --> 01:06:24.463
Yeah well...


01:06:24.543 --> 01:06:26.276
You're not the one
I'm worried about.


01:06:30.181 --> 01:06:31.570
I'm not crazy.


01:06:31.650 --> 01:06:33.283
In case you were wondering.


01:06:35.453 --> 01:06:37.988
I mean, yeah. But no.


01:06:38.389 --> 01:06:39.422
Not really.


01:06:51.202 --> 01:06:52.569
It started off as a joke.


01:06:53.604 --> 01:06:55.505
But just, saying it,


01:06:56.140 --> 01:06:57.307
I'm dying.


01:06:57.575 --> 01:06:58.497
Finite.


01:06:58.577 --> 01:07:01.644
It gave things
a sense of urgency.


01:07:04.482 --> 01:07:06.349
And sometimes it doesn't work.


01:07:07.284 --> 01:07:09.119
Well, most of the time.


01:07:11.655 --> 01:07:13.478
But there are days,


01:07:13.558 --> 01:07:16.092
if I really let myself
buy into it,


01:07:17.061 --> 01:07:18.617
where I can actually see


01:07:18.697 --> 01:07:21.164
the beauty of how little time
we actually have.


01:07:25.536 --> 01:07:26.636
And lately,


01:07:28.172 --> 01:07:30.473
that only seems to be happening
when I'm with you.


01:08:01.338 --> 01:08:02.806
What the hell are we?


01:08:05.242 --> 01:08:06.276
I don't know.


01:08:09.346 --> 01:08:10.480
I think that's okay.


01:08:12.083 --> 01:08:13.038
Me too.


01:08:13.118 --> 01:08:15.741
But we should make some rules.


01:08:15.821 --> 01:08:18.143
Rules?
Yeah.


01:08:18.223 --> 01:08:22.147
If we're gonna proceed with this
whole, star-crossed, platonic,


01:08:22.227 --> 01:08:24.461
g-rated, tragicomedy


01:08:25.129 --> 01:08:26.618
of ours,


01:08:26.698 --> 01:08:30.055
we should be very clear on what
we can and can't do.


01:08:30.135 --> 01:08:31.723
That's actually not a bad idea.
Which makes sense,


01:08:31.803 --> 01:08:34.393
'cause I only have good ones.
So... what?


01:08:34.473 --> 01:08:35.638
Rule number one:


01:08:36.574 --> 01:08:38.563
Nothing sexual and...
Yep. Agreed.


01:08:38.643 --> 01:08:41.244
I wasn't finished.
I am sorry.


01:08:41.879 --> 01:08:43.646
Nothing sexual in nature.


01:08:44.415 --> 01:08:46.338
Although, I mean.


01:08:46.418 --> 01:08:49.608
I can't just turn off
my natural appeal.


01:08:49.688 --> 01:08:52.277
I mean...
There's a lot going on here.


01:08:52.357 --> 01:08:54.579
And you're just gonna have to
learn to view it as a work of art


01:08:54.659 --> 01:08:57.749
in a museum that you can view and
appreciate but you know never...


01:08:57.829 --> 01:09:00.185
And you, quite frankly...
I'm sorry.


01:09:00.265 --> 01:09:02.821
Are gonna have to stop dressing
so suggestively.


01:09:02.901 --> 01:09:04.134
I know.


01:09:05.369 --> 01:09:07.626
Rule number two...
Uh-uh my turn.


01:09:07.706 --> 01:09:10.562
But I...
I get to make some rules.


01:09:10.642 --> 01:09:12.375
Okay, but mine was gonna
be good.


01:09:14.678 --> 01:09:15.745
Rule number two:


01:09:17.448 --> 01:09:21.251
We let ourselves be friends.


01:09:23.287 --> 01:09:24.420
Without shame.


01:10:31.356 --> 01:10:33.311
<i>Could be a bit tight.</i>


01:10:33.391 --> 01:10:35.514
But for having three baptisms
in a week,


01:10:35.594 --> 01:10:37.649
I think we found
a really nice job.


01:10:37.729 --> 01:10:38.817
What about Friday?


01:10:38.897 --> 01:10:41.753
Friday?
Yeah. Night.


01:10:41.833 --> 01:10:45.635
If I have this correct I think we
should all be free at that time.


01:10:46.470 --> 01:10:48.426
For what?
Dinner.


01:10:48.506 --> 01:10:53.309
No offense, but we already eat
together like 15 times a week.


01:10:54.645 --> 01:10:57.302
I also have a reservation for
the golden corral,


01:10:57.382 --> 01:10:58.637
which I'm not gonna miss.


01:10:58.717 --> 01:11:00.283
They take reservations?


01:11:01.285 --> 01:11:03.720
No. No Daniel, they don't.


01:11:04.788 --> 01:11:06.511
What's going on Friday?


01:11:06.591 --> 01:11:08.213
I just thought that
we could all have dinner.


01:11:08.293 --> 01:11:09.681
Together. At the rectory.


01:11:09.761 --> 01:11:11.894
Oh yeah, no problem.
With a friend of mine.


01:11:14.298 --> 01:11:15.220
A friend?


01:11:15.300 --> 01:11:19.636
If this friend is
as fun as you two,


01:11:20.537 --> 01:11:21.459
well, count me in.


01:11:21.539 --> 01:11:23.806
She is fun. Great.


01:11:24.508 --> 01:11:25.541
Fun and great.


01:11:27.378 --> 01:11:28.411
She?


01:11:29.647 --> 01:11:31.436
She. Yes.


01:11:31.516 --> 01:11:34.539
She's a she. Jane is her name.
It's a female name.


01:11:34.619 --> 01:11:37.954
Which she has because she's
a girl. Woman.


01:11:41.292 --> 01:11:43.459
Well, to be clear,


01:11:45.663 --> 01:11:48.631
I'm definitely available
for this dinner now.


01:12:14.858 --> 01:12:16.025
I like the bread.


01:12:17.361 --> 01:12:19.429
- Thanks.
- Yes, Daniel.


01:12:19.963 --> 01:12:21.353
Bread is quite good.


01:12:21.433 --> 01:12:22.454
It's brioche.


01:12:22.534 --> 01:12:23.755
I didn't realize you baked.


01:12:23.835 --> 01:12:25.857
Oh no. I bought it.


01:12:25.937 --> 01:12:27.592
Well, it's really good.


01:12:27.672 --> 01:12:28.860
Still.


01:12:28.940 --> 01:12:31.574
For store bought
it's really good.


01:12:32.076 --> 01:12:33.409
Pasta's good too.


01:12:34.111 --> 01:12:36.034
You bought the pasta as well?


01:12:36.114 --> 01:12:38.503
Nope. Nope. I made that. Myself.


01:12:38.583 --> 01:12:41.384
- Old family recipe.
- Oh.


01:12:42.019 --> 01:12:42.941
Ollie.


01:12:43.021 --> 01:12:50.048
You being a connoisseur
of all things, remotely edible,


01:12:50.128 --> 01:12:53.863
I'd love to have
your expert opinion on the meal.


01:12:55.432 --> 01:12:57.033
It's hilarious.
I'm sorry?


01:12:58.902 --> 01:13:00.558
Very good. It's delicious.


01:13:00.638 --> 01:13:02.627
Excellent effort.
I'm proud of you.


01:13:02.707 --> 01:13:05.730
Thank you. I always felt like
I should cook more, you know?


01:13:05.810 --> 01:13:08.111
I agree. And the best part
of cooking more...


01:13:10.414 --> 01:13:11.614
Is more dinner guests.


01:13:12.049 --> 01:13:14.484
Umm... thanks.


01:13:15.152 --> 01:13:16.519
No. Thank you.


01:13:17.855 --> 01:13:21.724
And thank you for introducing us
to Jenny.


01:13:22.626 --> 01:13:23.659
Jane.


01:13:24.461 --> 01:13:25.661
What did I say?


01:13:26.163 --> 01:13:27.163
Not Jane.


01:13:29.166 --> 01:13:30.822
Strawberry shortcake
for dessert.


01:13:30.902 --> 01:13:33.736
So, you know, gotta save room.


01:13:35.739 --> 01:13:37.996
And ice cream.
Sponge or pound?


01:13:38.076 --> 01:13:39.142
What?


01:13:39.977 --> 01:13:41.566
Sponge cake or pound cake


01:13:41.646 --> 01:13:43.335
as the base?


01:13:43.415 --> 01:13:45.003
You know, it's called
strawberry shortcake,


01:13:45.083 --> 01:13:47.706
but I never really considered
strawberry shortcake


01:13:47.786 --> 01:13:51.076
unless it has a pound cake
or a sponge cake as the base.


01:13:51.156 --> 01:13:53.478
Not that biscuit thing


01:13:53.558 --> 01:13:56.092
that my grandmother used to always
try to pass off as dessert.


01:13:57.461 --> 01:13:59.084
Well, traditionally speaking,


01:13:59.164 --> 01:14:05.101
shortcake is really supposed to
be more savory, less sweet.


01:14:06.437 --> 01:14:07.992
A fun fact.


01:14:08.072 --> 01:14:11.563
Especially if you decide
you want to do your own baking.


01:14:11.643 --> 01:14:13.898
I definitely prefer sponge cake.


01:14:13.978 --> 01:14:16.746
Oh. That's your god given right.


01:14:17.181 --> 01:14:18.703
And there is um...


01:14:18.783 --> 01:14:23.508
Certainly others who feel
that it's less,


01:14:23.588 --> 01:14:26.489
uh, substantive. Empty.


01:14:26.924 --> 01:14:28.079
Fleeting.


01:14:28.159 --> 01:14:29.948
But it tastes better.


01:14:30.028 --> 01:14:31.783
Amen sister.


01:14:31.863 --> 01:14:33.885
And sure it might be wrapped
in cheap cellophane,


01:14:33.965 --> 01:14:35.698
shelf stable for like,


01:14:36.099 --> 01:14:37.822
a hundred years.


01:14:37.902 --> 01:14:39.724
Sadly placed somewhere between
little Debbie's


01:14:39.804 --> 01:14:41.726
and generic Twinkies rip-offs on
the shelf


01:14:41.806 --> 01:14:43.395
but at the end of the day,


01:14:43.475 --> 01:14:45.942
if it tastes better
than your other options,


01:14:46.543 --> 01:14:47.577
what can you do?


01:14:49.713 --> 01:14:51.013
Have better taste.


01:14:51.849 --> 01:14:53.483
Oh man. I forgot.


01:14:53.984 --> 01:14:56.252
There is no cake.


01:14:57.821 --> 01:14:59.477
There's no sponge cake.
There's no pound cake.


01:14:59.557 --> 01:15:01.123
There's no shortcake.
There's no cake.


01:15:03.727 --> 01:15:06.562
Got caught up in the
strawberries I guess.


01:15:07.731 --> 01:15:10.955
But yeah. Anyway.
There is ice cream.


01:15:11.035 --> 01:15:14.125
- Which everyone seems to enjoy so...
- Vanilla or chocolate?


01:15:14.205 --> 01:15:16.060
Can we just talk about dinner?


01:15:16.140 --> 01:15:17.929
The flavor...
Just for right now?


01:15:18.009 --> 01:15:19.464
Please. Thank you.


01:15:19.544 --> 01:15:20.832
That'd be great.


01:15:20.912 --> 01:15:23.713
So, Jane.
Did I say it right this time?


01:15:27.284 --> 01:15:28.284
Yes.


01:15:29.052 --> 01:15:30.842
Hmm. What do you do, Jane?


01:15:30.922 --> 01:15:32.855
Like, for a living?


01:15:33.724 --> 01:15:34.879
Sure.


01:15:34.959 --> 01:15:36.125
I'm a musician.


01:15:36.860 --> 01:15:38.183
Mostly at a coffee shop.


01:15:38.263 --> 01:15:40.596
Where I also sometimes work.


01:15:41.198 --> 01:15:42.921
Because I'm a musician.


01:15:43.001 --> 01:15:45.123
Mostly at a coffee shop.
Well would you say that,


01:15:45.203 --> 01:15:47.459
music is your passion?


01:15:47.539 --> 01:15:49.694
Um, well I mean, yeah.
It's a passion.


01:15:49.774 --> 01:15:51.040
Yeah. She's really good.


01:15:51.742 --> 01:15:53.031
Pretty great.


01:15:53.111 --> 01:15:55.311
We should go
check her out sometime.


01:15:56.046 --> 01:15:56.935
What does that mean?


01:15:57.015 --> 01:15:58.002
What does what mean?


01:15:58.082 --> 01:16:00.116
A passion.


01:16:00.918 --> 01:16:02.540
I mean,


01:16:02.620 --> 01:16:04.876
a person can have
more than one passion.


01:16:04.956 --> 01:16:07.056
Right?
You tell me.


01:16:08.559 --> 01:16:09.725
I think I just did.


01:16:12.563 --> 01:16:15.298
Daniel.
Uh, yeah. I think um...


01:16:16.800 --> 01:16:20.069
I think passion, you know,
has several different, uh...


01:16:21.972 --> 01:16:23.072
Like father Ollie.


01:16:23.874 --> 01:16:25.942
He likes, uh, carbohydrates.


